  "term": "Vineland Adaptive Behavior Scales",
  "definition": "The Vineland Adaptive Behavior Scales are a tool used to assess social functioning and everyday adaptive behaviors in people from preschool through age 18. The information is used to help support diagnosis of intellectual and developmental disabilities.",
